From 79ca837a0364efbc044034367db18d6312c55610 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:30:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 83/85] hw/display: LCD mini Click (MCP23S17, MCP4161, 16x2
 character LCD)

"click-lcdmini" (LCD mini Click v101 with the LCD mini display, a Topway
LMB162XFW with an ST7066U):
- an MCP23S17 on SPI, the Mcp23x17 core behind SPI framing (opcode,
  address, data; address bits checked with IOCON.HAEN), RESET# on RST,
  INTB on INT;
- port B drives the LCD: RS GPB2, E GPB3, DB4-DB7 GPB4-GPB7, DB0-DB3 and
  R/W tied low;
- the ST7066U/HD44780 instruction set from an 8-bit power-on state:
  latches on falling E, 4-bit transfers after function set, clear,
  home, entry mode, display control with cursor and blink (409 ms),
  cursor and display shift, CGRAM and DDRAM (two lines of 40 or one of
  80); execution times not modelled;
- an MCP4161 on its own chip select (AN) sets the contrast with its
  volatile wiper (write, increment, decrement); the backlight is on
  unless PWM is driven low;
- a PpPanel picture: 5x8 dot cells, codes 00h-0Fh from CGRAM and 20h-7Fh
  in a 5x7 font with the A00 ROM's yen and arrows, white on blue as the
  product photograph shows, its strength following the wiper, blocks on
  the first line until the first instruction; "text", "contrast" and
  "backlight-on" for tests and front ends.

qtests: MikroElektronika's start-up (02h into 4-bit mode), two lines of
text, a display shift, the contrast write and the backlight on the
MC00's EXT1; text through SPI0 on the AVR64EA48 Nano Base.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
