+/*
+ * LCD mini Click: a 16x2 character LCD behind an MCP23S17
+ *
+ * Peripheral Pretender: a personal project. AI-assisted code;
+ * not for submission to upstream QEMU.
+ *
+ * LCD mini Click (MikroElektronika, schematic v101) with its LCD mini
+ * display (Topway LMB162XFW, an ST7066U controller):
+ *  - An MCP23S17 on SPI (CS# with R4 10 kOhm pull-up, A2..A0 on ground,
+ *    RESET# on RST, INTB on INT) drives the LCD from port B: RS on GPB2,
+ *    E on GPB3, DB4-DB7 on GPB4-GPB7. DB0-DB3 are tied to ground and R/W
+ *    to ground, so the LCD is write-only and its busy flag unreadable.
+ *    The register file, pads and interrupts are the Mcp23x17 core's
+ *    (hw/gpio/mchp_mcp23x17.c); SPI frames are an opcode (0100 A2 A1 A0
+ *    R/W, the address bits checked only with IOCON.HAEN), the register
+ *    address, then data at the advancing pointer.
+ *  - An MCP4161 digital potentiometer (CS# on AN with R5 10 kOhm pull-up)
+ *    sets the LCD's contrast voltage from its wiper (DS22059B section
+ *    7: 16-bit commands AD3:AD0 C1:C0 D9:D8 then D7:D0, write C = 00;
+ *    8-bit increment C = 01 and decrement C = 10; wiper 0 is address 0,
+ *    0-256, mid-scale at power-on). Only the volatile wiper is modelled;
+ *    the MCP4161 has no SDO line on the Click. MikroElektronika's driver
+ *    writes 255 - contrast: a low wiper is a dark display.
+ *  - The backlight is switched by a transistor from PWM, R1 1 kOhm
+ *    pulling it on.
+ *  - The ST7066U follows the HD44780's instruction set: it starts in
+ *    8-bit mode, one line, display off; each falling E latches DB7-DB0
+ *    (a nibble at a time, high first, once function set picks 4 bits),
+ *    RS choosing data or instruction. Clear, home, entry mode, display
+ *    on/off with cursor and blink, cursor and display shift, function
+ *    set, CGRAM and DDRAM addresses, data to DDRAM (two lines of 40 at
+ *    00h and 40h, or one of 80) or CGRAM. Execution times are not
+ *    modelled. The panel shows codes 00h-0Fh from CGRAM, 20h-7Fh in a
+ *    5x7 font with the A00 ROM's yen and arrows, and nothing for the
+ *    ROM's other codes. Until the first instruction the first line shows
+ *    blocks, as a powered, uninitialised module does.
+ *  - The picture: blue background, white dots (as the Click's product
+ *    photograph shows; the LMB162XFW manual describes a yellow-green
+ *    part), their strength following the contrast wiper, dim with the
+ *    backlight off. The window's size is estimated from the photograph.
+ * Not checked against a physical Click.
+ *
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+ */
+
